<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Axel Oxenstierna</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Axel Oxenstierna was Lord High Chancellor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from 1612 until his death in 1654. He worked closely with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a> to reform the central administration and led Swedish policy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War after the king's death. He is regarded as a principal architect of the governance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/axel-oxenstierna.jpg" alt="Axel Oxenstierna" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michiel Jansz. van Mierevelt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unknown_painter_after_M._van_Mierevelt_-_Portrait_of_Axel_Ochsenstierna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
